st time that Donald  Trump has done this after the Orlando  nightclub shooting he basically came out  and said see I was right  right about what who knows I mean what  does it even mean Jason to say this is  what I've been talking about that  there's gun violence that black people  will vote for you if anything bad  happens to them even if that has really  nothing to do with President Obama but  the permissive gun laws that we see  everywhere around the Chicago area I  think it just shows his absolute  disconnect with society and people in  general he has no humanity to him who  who in the right mind would say this  never mind  in person on the internet wherever is it  possible he thinks of this as outreach  to black people because he thinks oh  what was a black person died I've been  saying black people should vote for me  therefore I will tweet now black people  will vote for me I've admit maybe he's  so deluded that he thinks this is a way  to actually show that he would in some  way be good for the non-white  communities of the u.s. I'm really  trying to rationalize what cannot be  rationalized here yeah this is as close  as he gets to you know being humanizing  and connecting with black people in it I  think it goes further to show the point  that he's not actually trying to connect  with black people he's trying to connect  with certain white demographics to make  him seem like he's not a bad guy that's  right where he's gone with this I think  Dara Lindh wrote an article saying  exactly that which is this newfound  attempt at outreach to black people  which of course as we know I can't  imagine would convince a single black  person to vote for Trump it's more about  appealing to the moderate white voters  who have been turned off by Trump's  insane bigotry and racially tinged  language because you're not going to  convince any black people to vote for  you with this type of rhetoric but if  there are white people who don't like  Hillary and they hear anything